From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 15:54:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] AMLCapture: change the size of a running stream in place

A consumer that needed a larger size restarted the shared stream, and a
smaller one of the same inputs did too, which drops frames for every
reader of the engine. vdin takes a size with its turns and stamps each
frame with its size. Continuous streams move from MMAP to heap DMABUF
buffers, which can grow while the stream runs.
